  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 334 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nAfter Tuesday, synoptic guidance indicates that the upper-level \nridge will persist over the western half of the CONUS with \nincreasingly blocked flow behind a closed low developing over the \nEast Coast. Embedded shortwaves in the low-level flow towards the \nwest will increase PoPs through midweek, before a stronger impulse \nfrom the upper-level trough off the PNW Coast prompts the recession \nof the ridge off towards the west. This impulse in the upper-level \nflow is projected to dig southeastward, impacting the forecast area \nby the end of the period. There is continued variance in long term \nsolutions on the exact timing and placement of this feature, but \nthis variance is lessening with subsequent forecast cycles, so \ngreater confidence may be ascertained in this solution. However, \nconsidering how far in the future this forecast resides, this trend \nwill need to continue being monitored.",
